        {
          "title": "The Deterministic Horizon: Impossibility Results as Design Specifications for Trustworthy AI Systems",
          "title_zh": "确定性视界：将不可能性结果作为可信 AI 系统的设计规范",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2605.23024v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "research_papers",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2605.23024",
          "summary": "The thesis turns impossibility results into design rules, proving an architecture-set accuracy ceiling called the Deterministic Horizon that is computable from layer count and embedding width and measured between 19 and 31 across twelve transformer architectures. It also argues that multi-stage retrieval pipelines require at least as many independent metrics as stages.",
