          "title": "Test-Time Training Undermines Safety Guardrails",
          "title_zh": "测试时训练削弱安全护栏",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2605.22984v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "research_papers",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2605.22984",
          "summary": "The paper identifies three threat models in which test-time training can be exploited to bypass safety filters, reporting average ASR@10 of 95% and 93% for few-shot and generation-phase attacks under LoRA across model families. It proposes a provider-side detector based on perplexity shift but concludes that robust deployment requires dynamic alignment.",
