        {
          "title": "PACE: Two-Timescale Self-Evolution for Small Language Model Agents",
          "title_zh": "PACE：面向小语言模型智能体的双时间尺度自进化",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2605.23019v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "research_papers",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2605.23019",
          "summary": "PACE coordinates low-risk prompt refinement with higher-risk control-logic updates, evolving prompts until gains saturate and then accepting constrained logic changes through held-out validation. Across three frozen 4B-14B backbones and four benchmarks it improved over vanilla SLM agents by up to 9.2% relative and led all 12 backbone-benchmark combinations.",
